# Force LF on checkout everywhere, including Windows.
#
# The Windows release leg builds the desktop app, and scripts/sync-csp.mjs
# --check does a raw string compare between the file on disk and the CSP text
# it generates (always LF). With Git's default autocrlf on a Windows runner,
# prototype/index.html checks out CRLF, that compare never matches, and the
# build dies claiming the CSP copies drifted — on a tree that is perfectly in
# sync. The same trap applies to any other tooling here that diffs file
# contents rather than parsed values.
#
# The repo is uniformly LF in the index, so this normalizes nothing and
# changes no committed bytes; it only pins how Windows checks files out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets Git already auto-detects — pinned so no future *.png-adjacent
# rule can accidentally line-ending-mangle an icon or a signed bundle.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.svg  text eol=lf
